    "result_text": "Done. The change is complete and the full test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nReplaced the string `membershipTier` with a numeric `membershipLevel` (1\u20133), computed on creation.\n\n**Rule implemented:** start at 1; +1 when an email is present; +1 when `namesakeCount` is 0; capped at 3 (level 4 reserved for tenure). Note the old tier's `householdSize >= 3 \u2192 GOLD` branch is gone \u2014 level no longer depends on household size.\n\n**Files changed:**\n- `model/Owner.java` \u2014 added a derived, non-persisted `getMembershipLevel()` (`@Transient`) carrying the rule. Kept derived (like the old tier) since it's a pure function of already-stored `email` and `namesakeCount` \u2014 no DB schema change needed.\n- `mapper/OwnerMapper.java` \u2014 removed the `membershipTier` expression mapping; `membershipLevel` now auto-maps by name.\n- `resources/openapi.yml` \u2014 replaced the `membershipTier` (string) property with `membershipLevel` (integer, min 1 / max 3), so the generated `OwnerDto` drops tier in favour of level.\n- `rest/function/owner/AuditOwnerCreated.java` \u2014 the create audit line now records `membershipLevel=` instead of nothing tier-related.\n- `rest/function/owner/AssignHouseholdSize.java` \u2014 removed the now-stale javadoc reference to the GOLD tier.\n\n**Tests:** `AcceptanceTest.coreNumericLevel` passes (email + unique name \u2192 level 3), and the full `./mvnw test` suite reports `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
